<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15604" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτέομαι</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 Verb, 
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be prepared,
				make ready,</i> c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δὲ αὖτις πολεμέειν . . ἀρτέοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.120
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτέετο ἐς πόλεμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.97
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἳ οὐκ ἔων ναυμαχίην ἀρτέεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.143
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀν-, παρ-αρτέομαι.</span>
			Akin to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτίζομαι,</span> not to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτάομαι.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
